As present, there exist many things in Nethack that are practically
useless. The whip skill, for instance; the bullwhip does little
damage, cannot harm some monsters and the only profession that can use
them well is better off using a mattock or Grayswandir. Even more
useless is the iron chain - total uses are as follows: food for
metallivores, creation of steel golems (which can be polymorphed into
something more useful), and random curse bait.

A bit of a band-aid may be to make iron chains usable as whips! Given
their material, they'll be able to damage thick-skinned monsters, and
they should probably deal a higher amount of damage than the bullwhip
(and rubber hose). They can be used for all normal bullwhip purposes
(disarming, grabbing items, etc).

Ordinarily, I'd say this upsets the status quo, what with their few
drawbacks, except that 1) otherwise, the bullwhip skill is totally
useless, 2) they're hard to get until an amount of time into the game
anyway.

Of course, they;d have to be made into weapons (or weapon tools) to be
enchantable and effective armaments. I don't know how hard this would
be...though it's worth pointing out that they're in a class all their
own ("_", or "chains") which may or may not make it easier to modify
them appropriately.

Thoughts?



